From: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: bcm - start the next chunk after a fully used scatterlist entry

The driver splits a request larger than max_payload into several SPU
messages and keeps its place in the source and destination
scatterlists with spu_msg_sg_add(). When a message ends exactly at the
end of a scatterlist entry, spu_msg_sg_add() leaves from_sg on that
entry with from_skip 0 instead of moving to the next entry. The next
message then reads or writes the entry that was just used up, again
from its start.

On BCM6755, an AF_ALG encryption of 200000 bytes through
ecb-aes-iproc, cbc-aes-iproc or ctr-aes-iproc into a buffer at page
offset 0x30 hits this. The third 65520-byte message ends on a page
boundary of the destination, so the fourth message's output lands 4096
bytes early, at offset 192464 instead of 196560, and the last 3440
bytes of the result are never written. The same happens at 262144 and
300000 bytes. Decryption into a buffer at another page offset is
correct.

Move to the next entry when the copy ends on an entry boundary.

Fixes: 9d12ba86f818 ("crypto: brcm - Add Broadcom SPU driver")
Signed-off-by: Ho Jie Feng <hjf3108@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/crypto/bcm/util.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/crypto/bcm/util.c
+++ b/drivers/crypto/bcm/util.c
@@ -161,8 +161,11 @@ u32 spu_msg_sg_add(struct scatterlist **to_sg,
 			/* used up all of from entry */
 			skip = 0;	/* start at beginning of next entry */
 		}
-		if (copied == length)
+		if (copied == length) {
+			if (frag_len == entry_len)
+				sg = sg_next(sg);
 			break;
+		}
 	}
 	*to_sg = to;
 	*from_sg = sg;
